  "id": "COMPOUND:15051 - PROTEIN:3763",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Ludongnin G may interact with Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 9 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Ludongnin G to Werner syndrome ATP-dependent helicase, which is targeted by 1-Heptadecene, and this compound further targets the disintegrin domain-containing protein. The second pathway connects Ludongnin G to EDD domain protein, DegV family, which is targeted by 2,2'-Bithiophene, 5-(3-buten-1-ynyl)-5'-methyl-, and this compound also targets the disintegrin domain-containing protein. The third pathway shows Ludongnin G targeting EDD domain protein, DegV family, which is targeted by Chloramultiol C, which in turn targets the disintegrin domain-containing protein. These findings collectively indicate that Ludongnin G may act as a modulator of the disintegrin domain-containing protein through different biochemical intermediates. The evidence supports a potential role for Ludongnin G in influencing the activity of this protein, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
